Package: com.albrhi.carplay
Name: Albrhi CarPlay (rootless)
Version: 0.3.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: Run other apps on the CarPlay dashboard, and keeps your car's speakers in high quality while Camera is recording. Arabic or English.
 .
 ▍APPS ON THE DASHBOARD
 Add a bundle identifier in Settings › Albrhi CarPlay and that app's real interface
 appears on the CarPlay screen the next time it opens, instead of a cut-down template
 screen. Known to work on iOS 16 and 17; iOS 18 moved CarPlay's admission check
 somewhere this cannot reach yet without an on-disk patch this release does not make.
 .
 ▍THE RECORDING-AUDIO PROBLEM
 CarPlay audio is playing over your car's speakers. Camera opens, recording starts, and the
 music suddenly sounds like a phone call — because the instant a microphone is needed too,
 iOS drops Bluetooth to the phone-call profile, which is the only one that carries both
 directions at once.
 .
 ▍THE FIX
 Output and input are asked for separately: the car's speakers are kept on the
 high-quality profile, and the recording uses the iPhone's own microphone instead of
 sharing the car's. Both are ordinary, documented iOS audio settings — nothing here reads
 or changes anything about the call itself.
 .
 ▍NOT VALIDATED ON-DEVICE
 Built and checked, reasoned from public documentation and from reading two open-source
 references' architecture, but never run against a real CarPlay head unit. Treat the
 first install as a test, and leave the bridged-apps list empty to keep only the
 recording-audio fix.
 .
 Developed by Ibrahim Ismail AL-Rahn. Free and open source under the GNU GPL v3. The
 recording-audio approach uses only public, documented AVAudioSession API; the app-display
 role rewrite hooks two public UIKit selectors for a purpose Apple did not intend.
